# Design documents and research notes are internal working material. The
# normative roadmap, the reader-facing implementation notebook and the README
# figures are deliberately tracked exceptions.
docs/*
!docs/roadmap.md
!docs/evoir-spec.md
!docs/evomir-spec.md
!docs/lean-plan.md
!docs/status.md
!docs/notebook/
!docs/notebook/**
!docs/images/
!docs/images/**
lessons.md

# Runtime evidence is machine-generated output, not source.
# Evidence directories are large, host-specific, and reproducible by re-running
# the acceptance harnesses; the repository tracks the harnesses, not the runs.
.evidence/

# Signed third-party installer payloads are pinned by digest inside contracts.
# Tracking the binaries themselves would bloat history without adding trust.
*.pkg

# Pinned toolchains, kernel trees, and build outputs are fetched or produced
# by the harness. Only the bulky derived state is ignored; the build recipes
# and the small digest records that contracts reference are tracked source.
.toolchain/artifacts/
.build/

# Correspondence vectors and the answers each side writes beside them. Both are
# regenerated from tools/lean/vectors.py and a fixed seed; a tracked copy would
# be a second thing to keep in step with the generator, and the sets run to tens
# of megabytes.
lean/vectors/

# Rust build artifacts.
target/
target-*/

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
.claude/worktrees/

# Python bytecode caches.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
output/
